          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.213,
            0.745,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The air which surrounds the Earth is a mixture of gases. Can you name some gases which are present in the air? Air contains nitrogen, oxygen, argon, carbon dioxide and other gases in small quantities. Fig. 11.1 gives the composition of air in percentage. Notice that in Fig. 11.1 there are 100 squares. Out of 100 squares, 78 are occupied by nitrogen, 21 are occupied by oxygen, and 1 by argon, carbondioxide and other gases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.4,
            0.567,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Percentage is the number of parts in 100. It is denoted by the symbol ‘%’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.681,
